                },
                {
                    "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
                },
                {
                    "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
                    "markdown": "Inspect running processes on an iPhone or iPad running custom firmware. Monitor CPU usage, memory, and threads, then open a process for more detail.\n\n## Features\n\n- Follow a live process list with updates every second, or pause it to inspect a moment in time.\n- Search by name or PID, sort the list, and filter system, user, or app processes.\n- Inspect threads, open files and sockets, Mach ports, loaded modules, sandbox status, and disk and network use.\n- Ask a process to quit or force it to quit. PID 1 cannot be stopped.\n- Share a snapshot of a process as a file.\n- Inspect and monitor processes from a terminal with `inspector`.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nRequires iOS 15 or later and custom firmware with a roothide or rootless bootstrap. Choose the `iphoneos-arm64e` package for roothide or `iphoneos-arm64` for rootless.\n\n[View Source](https://github.com/owngoal-dev/Inspector) · [Join the Community](https://discord.gg/vqhDEep2mN)",
                    "useSpacing": true
                },
